---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Methane Outliers Map" path="/map/">
  <header class="masthead">
    <div>
      <h1>Alberta and Texas, one lens</h1>
      <p class="tagline">
        Every producing reporting unit in both jurisdictions &mdash;
        Alberta facilities and Texas leases &mdash; colored by the same
        apples-to-apples measure: <strong>flared+vented gas as a share
        of gas-equivalent production</strong>, over each unit&rsquo;s
        latest 12-month window. Dot size is flared+vented volume.
      </p>
    </div>
    <span class="window-badge" id="window-badge" hidden></span>
  </header>

  <section class="tiles" id="tiles" aria-label="Headline comparison"></section>

  <div class="controls">
    <div class="legend" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="legend-title">Flared+vented / production</span>
      <span class="swatch" style="--c: var(--seq-150)"></span><span>&lt;0.1%</span>
      <span class="swatch" style="--c: var(--seq-300)"></span><span>0.1&ndash;1%</span>
      <span class="swatch" style="--c: var(--seq-450)"></span><span>1&ndash;5%</span>
      <span class="swatch" style="--c: var(--seq-550)"></span><span>5&ndash;20%</span>
      <span class="swatch" style="--c: var(--seq-700)"></span><span>&gt;20%</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <main class="layout">
    <div id="map" class="map-box" role="application"
      aria-label="Combined jurisdiction map"></div>
    <aside class="panel">
      <h2>Reading this honestly</h2>
      <p class="panel-note" style="font-size: 0.84rem">
        The two regimes report differently &mdash; different rules,
        different measurement, and both under-report against satellite
        observation &mdash; so absolute levels are not a scoreboard.
        What this view compares fairly: the same physical ratio,
        computed the same way, over the same window length. Units with
        no production in the window (gas plants, gathering systems)
        are not shown. Alberta volumes are converted at
        1 e3m&sup3; = 35.3147 MCF.
      </p>
      <table class="outliers" id="worst">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Highest intensity, material volumes</th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">MMcf</th>
            <th scope="col" class="num">%</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody></tbody>
      </table>
    </aside>
  </main>

  <p slot="footer">
    Alberta: information licensed from Petrinex; data &copy; Government
    of Alberta. Texas: Railroad Commission of Texas public data.
    Non-commercial demonstration; derived statistics only.
  </p>

  <script src="../scripts/combined.js"></script>
</Base>
